  "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ we use the rule\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{\u2032}(\\theta )}{{x}^{\u2032}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{10{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )}{-10{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
